Linux is a kernel, not a complete OS.

Think of it like this:

Kernel = the core/engine of an operating system.
Operating System (OS) = Kernel + tools + libraries + utilities + applications, etc.

=> So what is Linux?

Linux = Kernel

The Linux kernel manages things like:

CPU
RAM
Hard disk
Network
Processes
Hardware devices

For example:

User
  ↓
Applications
  ↓
Shell / System tools
  ↓
Linux Kernel
  ↓
Hardware

=> Then what is Ubuntu?

Ubuntu is an Operating System (Linux distribution).

It contains:

Ubuntu
 ├── Linux Kernel
 ├── Shell (bash)
 ├── System utilities
 ├── Libraries
 ├── Package manager (apt)
 └── Other software

Similarly:

Ubuntu → OS / Linux distribution
RHEL → OS / Linux distribution
Rocky Linux → OS / Linux distribution
Debian → OS / Linux distribution
Linux → Kernel

=> Linux kernel = Engine

Ubuntu/RHEL = Complete car
